		{
			"id": "110635013326879230",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@timsev/110635013297249389",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tim Severien",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@timsev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/338/141/483/533/original/253f6de61dd10af0.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T20:18:50.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It doesn’t needs to be if it isn’t running in the browser. The issue is everyone bundling node(!) modules into codebases with browser as a target. It’s not as if we’re targeting different architectures that are functionally virtually identical.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635039487799012",
			"parentId": "110635013326879230",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110635039487799012",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T20:25:30.464Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@timsev\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>timsev</span></a></span> but we *needed* isomorphic JavaScript for single page applications, right? 🫣</p><p>…right?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635146563453382",
			"parentId": "110635039487799012",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@timsev/110635146540451515",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tim Severien",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@timsev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/288/338/141/483/533/original/253f6de61dd10af0.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T20:52:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> In the early days, SPA’s were exclusively client-side and could’ve worked fine with a browser-specific package manager (like bower). I think it was node.js folk that pursued isomorphism, and devs that built JS-heavy sites followed naturally.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635150038869988",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://cathode.church/@easrng/110635149823274143",
			"author": {
				"name": "easrng :heart_cyber_pink:",
				"url": "https://cathode.church/@easrng",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T20:53:34.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> But unlike CommonJS ~nobody ships JSX or TypeScript files on NPM directly.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635170102918752",
			"parentId": "110635150038869988",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110635170102918752",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T20:58:43.497Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://cathode.church/@easrng\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>easrng</span></a></span> I agree with the premise of the article! My point is that we should apply that premise to JSX too.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635196495530663",
			"parentId": "110635170102918752",
			"url": "https://cathode.church/@easrng/110635196132313027",
			"author": {
				"name": "easrng :heart_cyber_pink:",
				"url": "https://cathode.church/@easrng",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T21:05:20.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> right, my point is that JSX is completely optional since your dependencies won't use it and you can avoid using it by either calling your framework's <code>h</code> yourself or using something like <a href=\"https://npm.im/htm\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">htm</a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635266384304640",
			"parentId": "110635196495530663",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110635266384304640",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T21:23:12.630Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://cathode.church/@easrng\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>easrng</span></a></span> if JSX had been architected to use tagged template literals (a la htm), I would have no complaints—but alas, it was not. What I’m hearing is that you’re fine with transpilers for JSX—I wish they weren’t necessary.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635274653718099",
			"parentId": "110635266384304640",
			"url": "https://cathode.church/@easrng/110635274564567049",
			"author": {
				"name": "easrng :heart_cyber_pink:",
				"url": "https://cathode.church/@easrng",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T21:25:17.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> no i'm saying jsx is completely optional. there is ~no scenario in which you are required to use jsx, since it's just syntax sugar for <code>h</code> calls.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110635320764792471",
			"parentId": "110635274653718099",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/110635320764792471",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-06-30T21:37:02.409Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://cathode.church/@easrng\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>easrng</span></a></span> ehhh, I see what you mean—but saying that you don’t need to use JSX because someone else already ran the transpiler isn’t quite a strong enough argument for me to board that train of thought.</p><p>we needn’t belabor it further though, thanks for the chat!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110648670931971135",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://types.pl/@toastal/110648670893656076",
			"author": {
				"name": "ｔｏ⟁ｓｔ⟁ｌ",
				"url": "https://types.pl/@toastal",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-07-03T06:12:09.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> we don't need JSX, functions were always simpler and didn't require a compile step.</p>",
